  "name": "Reticulocyte Count",
  "code": "\tRETIC",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul><li>A reticulocyte count test measures the percentage of immature red blood cells (reticulocytes) in the blood. This test is used to evaluate the bone marrow's ability to produce new red blood cells and to monitor the effectiveness of treatments for conditions such as anemia.<br></li><li>A high reticulocyte count may indicate that your bone marrow is producing more red blood cells than normal, which can occur in response to anemia, bleeding, or certain medications.&nbsp;</li><li>A low reticulocyte count may indicate that your bone marrow is not producing enough red blood cells, which can be a sign of bone marrow damage or other underlying medical conditions.<br></li></ul>",
